# Project Development Standards

## UI & Components

* Use **shadcn/ui** components whenever an appropriate component exists.
* Prefer existing shared/common components before creating new ones.
* Build reusable components when the same UI or logic is used in multiple places.
* Do not duplicate components or UI patterns unnecessarily.
* Keep presentation/UI components separate from business logic where practical.

## API & Data Logic

* Do not duplicate API calls, API services, mutations, or data-fetching logic.
* Before creating new API logic, check whether an existing service, hook, query, mutation, or utility can be reused.
* Keep API/data-fetching logic separate from presentation components.
* Reuse existing types, schemas, services, and hooks whenever possible.

## Project Structure

* Follow the existing project folder structure and conventions.
* Before creating a new folder, component, hook, service, utility, or type, check how similar functionality is already organized.
* Follow existing naming conventions rather than introducing new patterns.
* Prefer consistency with the existing codebase over introducing a new architecture.

## Code Changes

* Make the smallest change necessary to solve the requested problem.
* Do not refactor unrelated code unless it is required for the task.
* Do not introduce a new dependency when an existing dependency or native solution is sufficient.
* Preserve existing behavior unless the task explicitly requires changing it.
* Before implementing something new, search the codebase for existing solutions.

## Quality

* Keep implementations simple, maintainable, and production-ready.
* Avoid unnecessary abstractions.
* Avoid premature optimization.
* Consider responsive behavior and accessibility for UI changes.
* Follow existing error handling and loading-state patterns.

## Important

When unsure whether to create something new, first look for an existing component, hook, service, utility, type, schema, or pattern that can be reused.
